Third-party data and services
=============================

1) internal/locs/data/celestials.tsv.gz — 星体名索引
   Derived from CCP hf's EVE Online Static Data Export (SDE), specifically the
   `mapDenormalize` table, via the community mirror published by Fuzzwork
   (https://www.fuzzwork.co.uk/dump/). Only four columns are kept
   (itemID, solarSystemID, groupID, itemName) for celestial objects inside solar
   systems; the file is gzip-compressed.
   Regenerate with: ./tools/build-celestials.sh [path/to/mapDenormalize.csv]
   EVE Online, its data and lore are properties of CCP hf. This project is an
   unofficial community tool and is not endorsed by or affiliated with CCP.

2) Runtime data sources
   - zKillboard R2Z2 sequence stream and API (https://r2z2.zkillboard.com,
     https://zkillboard.com/api/) — killmail feed and metadata.
   - EVE Swagger Interface / ESI (https://esi.evetech.net) — public read-only
     endpoints: universe names, killmails, routes.
   Both are consumed strictly read-only, with a descriptive User-Agent and
   conservative rate limits.

3) Ship renders / icons
   Served at runtime by /api/ship/{typeID}, proxied from CCP's image service
   (https://images.evetech.net) and cached locally under data/cache/ship/.
   No image files are redistributed in this repository.

4) Officials' ship-group list (internal/catalog/catalog.go, KnownGroups)
   Hand-maintained snapshot of ESI's "Entity" category groups whose names
   contain "Officer". The authoritative source at runtime is ESI itself
   (`/universe/categories/11/` + `/universe/groups/{id}/`).
